# Hexagonal Architecture

## Module Structure (Vertical Slicing)

Code is organized by **business modules**, not by technical layer (this is also known as screaming architecture)

### Structure of a Module

```
src/main/java/
└── com/example/[module-name]/
├── domain/           # Business core (no external dependencies)
│   ├── entities/
│   │   └── [Entity].java
│   ├── valueobjects/
│   │   └── [ValueObject].java
│   ├── services/
│   │   └── [DomainService].java
│   └── repositories/
│       ├── [Repository].java          # Interface
│       └── InMemory[Repository].java  # InMemory implementation
├── application/      # Use cases and ports for external services
│   ├── [UseCase].java
│   └── ports/
│       └── [ExternalService].java     # External service ports (driven)
├── infrastructure/   # Adapters (concrete implementations)
│   ├── adapters/
│   │   ├── [RepositoryImpl].java
│   │   └── [ApiClient].java
│   └── http/         # Primary port (driver)
│       └── [Controller].java
└── tests/            # Tests colocated within module
├── unit/         # Domain + UseCase tests
│   ├── [Entity]Test.java
│   ├── [ValueObject]Test.java
│   └── [UseCase]Test.java
├── integration/  # Repository adapter tests
│   └── [Repository]IntegrationTest.java
└── e2e/          # HTTP endpoint tests
└── [Controller]E2ETest.java
```

---

## Layers and Responsibilities

### 1. Domain (Center of the Hexagon)

- **Entities**: Objects with identity and lifecycle
- **Value Objects**: Immutable objects defined by their attributes
- **Domain Services**: Logic that doesn't belong to a specific entity
- **Repositories**: Interfaces + InMemory implementations for persisting/retrieving domain entities
- **DomainError**: Single error class with factory methods (see @.cursor/rules/design-errors.mdc)
- **No dependencies** towards application or infrastructure
- **No frameworks** or external libraries

### 2. Application (Use Cases)

- **Use Cases**: Orchestrate business logic
- **External Service Ports**: Interfaces for external services (email, payments, notifications)
- Depends **only** on Domain

### 3. Infrastructure (Adapters)

- **Adapters**: Concrete implementations of ports
- **Controllers/Handlers**: HTTP entry points, CLI, events
- Depends on Application and Domain
- **Frameworks and libraries live here**

---

## Dependency Rule

```
Infrastructure → Application → Domain
     ↓               ↓           ↓
  (Adapters)    (Use Cases)  (Entities)
```

- Dependencies **always point towards the center**
- Domain **never** imports from Application or Infrastructure
- Application **never** imports from Infrastructure

## Ports and Adapters

### Repositories (in Domain)

Repositories define contracts and include InMemory implementations in the same file.

```java
// src/main/java/com/example/invoices/domain/repositories/InvoiceRepository.java
package com.example.invoices.domain.repositories;

import com.example.invoices.domain.entities.Invoice;
import com.example.invoices.domain.valueobjects.Id;

import java.util.*;

public interface InvoiceRepository {
    void save(Invoice invoice);
    Optional<Invoice> findById(Id id);
    List<Invoice> findByCustomer(Id customerId);
}

export class InMemoryInvoiceRepository implements InvoiceRepository {
  private invoices: Map<string, Invoice> = new Map();
  // ... InMemory implementation
}

// src/main/java/com/example/invoices/domain/repositories/InMemoryInvoiceRepository.java
package com.example.invoices.domain.repositories;

import com.example.invoices.domain.entities.Invoice;
import com.example.invoices.domain.valueobjects.Id;

import java.util.*;

public class InMemoryInvoiceRepository implements InvoiceRepository {

    private final Map<String, Invoice> invoices = new HashMap<>();

    @Override
    public void save(Invoice invoice) {
        invoices.put(invoice.getId().getValue(), invoice);
    }

    @Override
    public Optional<Invoice> findById(Id id) {
        return Optional.ofNullable(invoices.get(id.getValue()));
    }

    @Override
    public List<Invoice> findByCustomer(Id customerId) {
        return invoices.values().stream()
                .filter(i -> i.getCustomerId().equals(customerId))
                .toList();
    }
}
```

### External Service Ports (in Application)

External services are use case needs, not domain needs.

```java
// src/main/java/com/example/invoices/application/ports/InvoiceNotifier.java
package com.example.invoices.application.ports;

import com.example.invoices.domain.entities.Invoice;
import com.example.invoices.domain.valueobjects.Id;

public interface InvoiceNotifier {
    void notifyInvoiceCreated(Invoice invoice);
    void notifyPaymentReceived(Id invoiceId);
}
```

### Implementing Adapters (in Infrastructure)

```java
// src/main/java/com/example/invoices/infrastructure/adapters/MongoInvoiceRepository.java
package com.example.invoices.infrastructure.adapters;

import com.example.invoices.domain.entities.Invoice;
import com.example.invoices.domain.repositories.InvoiceRepository;
import com.example.invoices.domain.valueobjects.Id;

import java.util.*;

public class MongoInvoiceRepository implements InvoiceRepository {

    @Override
    public void save(Invoice invoice) {
        // MongoDB implementation
    }

    @Override
    public Optional<Invoice> findById(Id id) {
        // MongoDB implementation
        return Optional.empty();
    }

    @Override
    public List<Invoice> findByCustomer(Id customerId) {
        // MongoDB implementation
        return List.of();
    }
}
```

```java
// src/main/java/com/example/invoices/infrastructure/adapters/EmailInvoiceNotifier.java
package com.example.invoices.infrastructure.adapters;

import com.example.invoices.application.ports.InvoiceNotifier;
import com.example.invoices.domain.entities.Invoice;
import com.example.invoices.domain.valueobjects.Id;

public class EmailInvoiceNotifier implements InvoiceNotifier {

    @Override
    public void notifyInvoiceCreated(Invoice invoice) {
        // Send email via SMTP/SendGrid/etc
    }

    @Override
    public void notifyPaymentReceived(Id invoiceId) {
        // Send payment confirmation email
    }
}
```

